# Development image for a board (profile q6a-dev): this file, empty of rules,
# replaces alsa-utils' rule of the same name, which runs `alsactl restore`
# when a sound card appears. On this board that restore turns the route to
# HDMI off (measured: the route on before it and off after, though the saved
# state has it on), and it runs at the moment mun-board-audio.service sets
# that route: when it came second, every write to the device failed (EIO)
# and the console started silent. Nothing here needs a saved mixer state:
# the route is the one setting, and board-audio-route sets it.
